  "question": {
    "text": "If the volume of a spherical ball is increasing at the rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cc</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>sec</mi></math>&nbsp;then the rate of increase of its radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>sec</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;when the volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>288</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cc</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;",
